{
  "name": "fresh-batch-same-id-is-an-error",
  "acceptance_item": 4,
  "note": "a fresh, valid batch — correctly echoing the newly issued generation 2, carrying a new reading — arrives under a batch id already acknowledged. A transport retry is same-bytes-same-id; this is a second look at the system, so it must be a recorded batch-id-reused protocol error with nothing applied. The defect this pins: an ack table that answered only 'seen' silently discarded every future acquisition from a collector minting stable batch ids, loop green.",
